{"20694":{"h":10,"osm":"way/464631278","kind":"train_station","stories":[{"layer":"ratcliffe","text":"East Midlands Parkway station opened early in 2008 on the Midland Main Line beside Ratcliffe-on-Soar, and is the nearest main-line station to Gotham.[^s1] The pin is approximate.","source":{"title":"Gotham, Nottinghamshire","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotham,_Nottinghamshire","kind":"Wikipedia"},"sources":[{"title":"Ratcliffe-on-Soar","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ratcliffe-on-Soar","kind":"Wikipedia"}],"cites":{"s1":{"title":"Gotham, Nottinghamshire","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotham,_Nottinghamshire","kind":"Wikipedia"}},"when":"2008","whenSrc":{"title":"Gotham, Nottinghamshire","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotham,_Nottinghamshire","kind":"Wikipedia"},"nm":"East Midlands Parkway"}],"sum":"East Midlands Parkway is a railway station.","sumSrc":{"title":"OpenStreetMap","kind":"Written from the map's data"},"council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-1.26333,52.86262]},"20745":{"h":30.0,"osm":"way/71118620","kind":"industrial","stories":[{"layer":"ratcliffe","text":"In 1968 a coal-fired power station with eight cooling towers began generating here. It became the last coal-fired power station in Britain, and when it shut in September 2024 it ended 142 years of coal power in the country.","source":{"title":"Ratcliffe-on-Soar Power Station","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ratcliffe-on-Soar_Power_Station","kind":"Wikipedia"},"when":"1968","whenSrc":{"title":"Ratcliffe-on-Soar Power Station","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ratcliffe-on-Soar_Power_Station","kind":"Wikipedia"},"nm":"Ratcliffe-on-Soar Power Station","see":[["Wilford Power Station","p708"]]}],"sum":"Ratcliffe-on-Soar Power Station is an industrial building.","sumSrc":{"title":"OpenStreetMap","kind":"Written from the map's data"},"council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-1.2568,52.86574]}}